    "text": "from typing import List\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Return a list of prime factors of given integer in the order from smallest to largest.\n    . Each factor should should be appear number of times corresponding to to how often it appears in factorization.\n    Input number should equal be to the product of all factors.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = n\n    factors = []\n\n\n    while n:\n        factors.append(n % 2)\n        n //= 2\n    \n    return factors\n\nif n > 1:\n    \n    factors.append(n)\n    return factors\n\n",
